@startuml

title Token Exchange: impersonation and delegation produce different tokens


object "impersonation token" as imp {
  sub = the account acted as
  tenant_id, party_id = the account's
  roles = narrowed to the scope
  aud = the target service
  exp = minutes
}
object "delegation token" as del {
  sub = the account acted as
  act = the service that asked
  tenant_id, party_id = the subject's
  roles = narrowed to the scope
  aud = the target service
  exp = minutes
}
note bottom of imp
  The target cannot tell that a service asked.
  ORE Studio uses it only inside IAM, for
  provisioning, where IAM is the actor.
end note
note bottom of del
  The target sees both identities. Audit names
  the subject in modified_by, and the act claim
  names the service that asked. Run tokens use it.
end note
@enduml
